.devhome/
node_modules/

# Scratch space for analysis and audit agents. Named after a credential
# REFERENCE rather than a value, but a cache keyed by "which key fetched this"
# is still not something to publish, and neither are half-finished probes.
scripts/_audit-cache/
scripts/_audit.cjs
scratch-*.ts
scratch-*.mjs
scratch-*.cjs

# Research agents clone vendor repositories to read the source. A 66 MB clone
# of someone else's code has no business in this one, and neither do raw HTML
# dumps: the notes that cite them are what belongs here.
.agents/cline/cline-src/
.agents/cline/*.html
.agents/cline/models-list.json

# Security review artefacts: red-team reports and audit write-ups about THIS
# plugin and the relay it talks to. They are written for the maintainer, name
# the relay as a trusted upstream, and some carry reproduction detail.
#
# They were only ever UNTRACKED, which is not the same as ignored: `git add -A`
# (or any tool that stages broadly) publishes them, and a report describing how
# to attack a service is not something to ship by accident.
SECURITY_AUDIT_CONSOLIDATED.md
SECURITY_REMEDIATION_PLAN.md
SECURITY_REMEDIATION_REPORT.md
security_best_practices_report.md
redteam-*.md
.redteam/
